  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 8ed86e343b81f2644816f268380ffef3, type: 3}
  m_Name: LorePart3
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::LoreData
  title: REPORT N.200520060610
  loreText: "Year 2005 \n\nThe Babylon Research Complex continued its efforts to
    stop the attacks of infected robots on the cities surrounding the Mirny-13 Exclusion
    Zone, but all attempts proved futile. Every time the scientists developed a new
    solution, the enemy adapted. The Generals would devise new tactics, and Mirium
    would immediately adjust its forces, creating countermeasures to prevent defeat.
    Everything changed when one of our exploration teams discovered an abandoned
    German military base dating back to World War II within one of the deeper phases
    of the subspace. It turned out that German scientists had also learned how to
    utilize Mirium for military and scientific purposes. They had begun developing
    a project known as \"Dark Edelweiss.\" The project's objective was the deployment
    of Mirium Gates at strategic attack points. These points could be established
    virtually anywhere\u2014on the front lines or deep behind enemy lines. It would
    have been the ultimate form of blitzkrieg warfare, perfected beyond anything
    previously imagined. However, the project never succeeded. The Germans required
    a special beacon capable of guiding personnel through the gates and back again.
    Because of this limitation, most of their facilities remained abandoned, while
    the majority of their personnel operated within the deepest phases of Mirny's
    subspace. What interested us most, however, were their experimental Mirium-based
    super-bombs. These devices possessed no destructive power in the conventional
    sense. Instead, they completely suppressed the properties of Mirium within the
    blast radius. This discovery could become the key to the success of all scientific
    and military efforts. \n\nJune 6, 2006 \n\nToday, we are deploying our final
    reconnaissance team to deliver a Mirium super-bomb and permanently seal the Gates.
    We still do not know what consequences this mission may have for the team. Mirium\u2014or
    whatever intelligence exists behind it\u2014may adapt to our strategy and find
    a way to prevent the mission from succeeding. \n\nJune 10, 2006 \n\nOur final
    reconnaissance team successfully delivered the bomb to the epicenter of the Fourth
    Phase and detonated it. Shortly after the explosion, the Mirny-13 Zone began
    to recover. The effects of Mirium gradually weakened, and the surrounding area
    slowly started returning to normal. At this time, the Babylon Research Complex
    has begun clearing the zone of remaining Mirium contamination and has temporarily
    placed the entire Mirny region under quarantine. The Complex will make every
    effort to ensure that both former and future residents can once again settle
    in the city and begin a new life. All inventions, devices, and technologies based
    on Mirium must be destroyed immediately. All research records are to be classified
    indefinitely. Today, we are relieved to report that we have finally shattered
    the twisted mirror that haunted our reality."
